Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:40:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 107/154] feat(profiles): reach one profile's own prefs by id
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three settings live in a Chromium profile rather than in spaces.json: search
suggestions, the download directory, and the default engine. This reads and
writes them for a profile named by id, refusing an id the bootstrap's own
allowlist rejects, since an id is a path component.

The page lookup is a separate target so it stays a fast unit rather than
needing a browser. A name this build does not know answers with an empty
string, so a caller drops the message instead of navigating somewhere it was
never asked to go.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 9eace827a2d41..c3d3121b25cec 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -3560,6 +3560,8 @@ static_library("ui") {
       "atrium/atrium_traffic_routing.h",
       "atrium/atrium_profile_bootstrap.h",
       "atrium/atrium_profile_bootstrap.cc",
+      "atrium/atrium_profile_prefs.h",
+      "atrium/atrium_profile_prefs.cc",
       "atrium/atrium_status_bubble_hook.h",
       "atrium/atrium_status_bubble_hook.cc",
       "atrium/atrium_sad_tab_hook.h",
